<title>UK: Guinness eases on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Guinness eases on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Guinness Plc eased on profit-taking even as the broad market shot up into record territory.</p>
<p>By 1201 GMT, the shares were off 9p to 475, on turnover of 2.87 million shares.  </p>
<p>Dealers said American investors, who had been snapping up the shares and contributed to the 13.5 percent advance in the share price since early February, seem to have disappeared.</p>
<p>&quot;The shares have had a good run. We're not seeing the buying from the States, so people took some profits,&quot; said one. -- London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
